  "id": "DrugBank_DB00684 - MONDO_2313",
  "verbalization": "Tobramycin, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is associated with Vernal Conjunctivitis through a multi-step pathway. The evidence suggests that Tobramycin may be used to treat Vernal Conjunctivitis by targeting inflammatory processes, as it is indicated for both Vernal Keratoconjunctivitis and Punctate Epithelial Keratoconjunctivitis. This pathway links Tobramycin to Loteprednol Etabonate, which is indicated for Vernal Conjunctivitis, indicating a potential role in modulating inflammation. Additionally, Tobramycin is directly linked to Vernal Keratoconjunctivitis, suggesting a possible therapeutic role in this condition. The integration of these pathways implies that Tobramycin may exert its effects through anti-inflammatory mechanisms, potentially involving the suppression of inflammatory mediators or the modulation of immune responses. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Tobramycin and Vernal Conjunctivitis, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
